>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Excl`

``` hol4
simpLib.Excl : string -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Excludes named rewrites, conversions and decision procedures from one
simplifier call.

Passing `Excl name` in the theorem list of a simplification conversion or
tactic has the effect of simplifying with `ss -* [name]`. The name is read
as follows:

- a name without dots, or of the form `name.` or `name.n` with `n` a
  numeral, is unqualified;
- `Thy.name` names `name` in theory `Thy`, which must be an ancestor of
  the current theory;
- `Thy.name.suffix` is read as theory `Thy` and name `name.suffix`.

This removes the rewrites derived from the theorem `name` (from the given
theory, if one is supplied), conversions named `name`, and the decision
procedure whose name is exactly the string given. Kernel-style names
(`Thy$name`) are not recognised.

### Failure

Never fails. The simplifier call fails if the theory is not an ancestor
or the name has more than two dots. A name that matches nothing is ignored.

### Example

``` hol4
>> SIMP_CONV bool_ss [] “p ∧ T”;
>> QCONV (SIMP_CONV bool_ss [Excl "bool.AND_CLAUSES"]) “p ∧ T”;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.SIMP_CONV`](#simpLib.SIMP_CONV),
[`simpLib.ExclX`](#simpLib.ExclX).
